.history
logs/
node_modules/
config.json
# ⚠️ THE BACKUPS HOLD THE SAME SECRETS AS THE ORIGINAL. config-writer.js and the connect-root-user
# util both drop `config.json.bak.<timestamp>` beside it before editing, and the bare `config.json`
# rule above does NOT match those names — so without this line a backup carrying root's password
# would sit in `git status` waiting for someone to `git add .`. Caught the same day the writer landed.
config.json.bak.*
.config.json.tmp-*
.vscode/